// BT-3054: exercises `self superclass` (backed by
// beamtalk_behaviour_intrinsics:classSuperclass/1, which calls
// beamtalk_object_class:module_name_safe/1) inside a block that executes in
// a foreign class's process (ADR 0109) — same shape as bt3052_parent.bt's
// `self new class`, but for the classSuperclass/1 call site migrated to
// module_name_safe/1 in this PR rather than class_of_object_by_name/1
// (BT-3052's own fix). `self` here is the class object itself
// (closure-captured via `ClassSelf`, per BT-3047).
//
// The corresponding test compares the result to the Symbol `#BT3047Ancestor`
// rather than the class object `BT3047Ancestor` — see BT-3057 (filed during
// this test's development): a class-object (`#beamtalk_object{}`) returned
// out of a class method, via any return path, currently degrades to a bare
// Symbol carrying the class's name, independent of this PR's changes. That
// Symbol is still a faithful witness that `classSuperclass/1` resolved the
// *correct* class (not a deadlock hang, not the wrong class) via
// module_name_safe/1, which is what this test targets.

BT3047Ancestor subclass: BT3054Parent

  class makeSelfSuperclassThrough: aDriverClass over: aList :: List =>
    aDriverClass
      run: [:x |
        result := self superclass
        ^result
      ]
      over: aList
    #wrong
